Subject: [PATCH] Rules: workstream 09's capacity kernel in the program's shape
 (capacity-preview) [skip ci]

permutation_rules::frontier::capacity, behind the new feature
capacity-preview (off by default: no default build code, vector, hash
input or budget changes): workstream 09's pools, grants and jobs as the
program will hold them, one pool account per facility generation (its
grants and an occupancy table, one row per job, so Reserve and Reclaim
read the pool alone) and one account per job; the fourteen operations
(OpenCapacityPool ... RetirePool, ClaimSplit as ClaimJob's split form),
each returning its events for the caller to log and to move the goods
they name; byte layouts with workstream 4's provisional AccountKind 25
and 26 and the proposed magic PSF1CPOL and PSF1CJOB.

workstreams/09-capacity/kernel/tests/rules_port.rs runs workstream 09's
kernel (the reference) and these rules side by side, the caller's part
(which job accounts, what a missing account means) written as the
program's handlers will: 6,000 random runs of 120 operations of every
kind, under all four policy mixes, captures and losses included, give
the same outcome, the same events, the same pool, jobs and Holding after
every step, and the accounts read back from their bytes. Two deliberate
breakages are caught (a capacity check off by one, a loss refunding a
refunded job); a third changed nothing because it is equivalent.

Undecided and unchanged: mixing sources, which resources lots hold, what
a seized vault's lots become; log kinds, magic and the build's version
(workstream 4).

